meta {
  name: Unsubscribe — One Click (signed link)
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/unsubscribe/one-click?email={{unsubEmail}}&t={{unsubToken}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  email: {{unsubEmail}}
  t: {{unsubToken}}
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
}

docs {
  RFC 8058 one-click unsubscribe, called directly by mail clients from the
  List-Unsubscribe header — so it is intentionally NOT behind the Bearer JWT.
  Authenticity comes from `t`, an HMAC-SHA256 of the lowercased email keyed by
  JWT_SECRET.

  To try it, set the `unsubEmail` / `unsubToken` environment variables using a
  link from a real confirmation email, or generate one:

      node -e 'console.log(require("crypto").createHmac("sha256", process.env.JWT_SECRET).update("you@example.com").digest("base64url"))'

  An invalid or missing token returns 400. GET on the same URL returns a small
  HTML confirmation page for humans who click the link.
}
